# crt-live: turns retro-crt from a still picture into a living monitor.
#
# Adds a full-screen group that asks kitty for a frame every 16 ms, and switches
# on the parts of retro-crt that need one: phosphor afterglow (trails fade in
# real time), animated snow, flicker, hum bar and hsync wobble.
#
# Cost: kitty redraws at ~60 fps for as long as the window is visible. Measured
# on the RTX 2070 laptop this holds the GPU at ~36 W instead of ~19 W, and the
# frame interval makes no difference (16, 33 and 50 ms all measured the same),
# so it is a state change, not a per-frame cost. Leave this file out of
# custom_shaders for a monitor that only redraws when text changes: ~0 W idle.
#
#   custom_shaders retro-crt crt-live

var int LIVE = 1

startgroup
    animation_step 16
    shaders retro-crt-pass
endgroup
